abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. For two-qubit states with steering-ellipsoid centre length c and Bob Bloch length r < 1, the attainable values of the three-setting correlation value F3^2 = ||T||_F^2 of arXiv:2406.03945 form exactly the interval [max(0, c(1+r)-1)^2, (1-r^2)(3-4c)+(c+(1-c)r)^2], with separable minimizers. For canonical states with radial support half-width t and squared correlation tau, the largest steering-ellipsoid volume is (4 pi/3)(t/2)min(tau-t^2, 1+2t+2t^2-c^2-tau), attained at every feasible triple. A filter succeeding with probability at least p in [1/2,1] can reveal F3 > 1 exactly when c < 2/(1+p+sqrt((1-p)^2+2)). Every one-sided filtering orbit is solved and the maximizers of the envelope are classified. Lean proves the central statements for actual density matrices. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
